<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Caribbean Fury #5 - Caribbean Cruise , 1994</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Caribbean Fury #5 Caribbean Cruise, 1994&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;1 April 1994, 1400 Zulu, 0900 Local&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Six weeks into the war, this is the&amp;nbsp;fifth and final scenario of a short campaign linked to the Northern Fury series, you may wish to refer to that background &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/blog/post19/"&gt;document&lt;/A&gt; to get a broader picture of the geopolitical setting. The situation in the &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/blog/post20/"&gt;Caribbean&lt;/A&gt; has fallen into something of a routine. Beyond an occasional Soviet submarine, the area has been quiet for over a month.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Of course, there is always one fly in the ointment, and here is it Venezuela. Rhetoric and accusations over the strike at Manodez Air Base, as well as strong evidence that Soviet submarines are replenishing at &lt;EM&gt;Puerto La Cruz &lt;/EM&gt;have fueled the tensions but so far, restraint has been shown by both sides.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Growing intelligence indicators, however, predict that this situation is about to change. Both Dutch and British sources are warning of a potential Venezuelan move on either Trinidad &amp;amp; Tobago or the Dutch ABC Islands (Aruba, Bonaire, and Curacao), or both. With NATO forces focused on protecting merchant shipping, the thought is that Venezuela will try for a quick grab at the islands and present the US with a &lt;EM&gt;fait accompli&lt;/EM&gt;, before standing down and offering a quick cessation of any hostilities.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You are commander of the newly re-established US 4&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Fleet with your flag aboard the newly re-commissioned &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;USS Albany (CG-10)&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;. The &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Albany&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; commissioned only nine months after the end of World War Two she has seen her share of sea miles, just like many of the ships under your command. Your primary task is to ensure the safety of merchant shipping gathering in convoy assembly areas, while still keeping a weather eye on Venezuela.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Background&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The Cold War continued with no thaw in relations. Germany’s reunification has caused friction between East &amp;amp; West. WP still alive and doing very well.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The Winter Olympics in Lillehammer turned into a fiasco when Soviet and eastern block teams failed to turn up for the opening ceremonies. Norway canceled the games and after some deliberation started to mobilize.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;War broke out across the globe around mid day on Sunday 13 Feb 94.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;In the Caribbean, Cuba, Honduras and Nicaragua joined the fray, somewhat haphazardly but for the first 18 hours had US and limited NATO forces were off balance. However, over the past weeks the situation has stabilized.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Cuba, reinforced by some high-end Soviet aircraft and SAM systems launched a devastating raid on Key West. Although there was some initial success, revenge was swift and a new government in Havana has called for a cease fire. Negotiations are ongoing but Cuban airspace is closed for NATO forces to allow the settlement to be finalized.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Honduras and Nicaragua have been nocked out of the war and the Guatemalan backed insurgency in Belize has been contained.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Designer’s notes&lt;/STRONG&gt;:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You should turn 'special messages' ON.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You will receive points for inflicting losses and preventing certain events from occurring.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;As the scenario begins, routine operations are ongoing. Merchant shipping will appear from the Panama Canal zone, the east coast of South America and the Gulf of Mexico (appearing south of Haiti). The shipping, which is not under your control, will gather at several convoy assembly points throughout the Greater Antilles.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Created by Bart Gauvin; AKA Gunner 98&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
